# What a clean checkout means for the first-user proof.
#
# BuildKit prefers `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` over the context's `.dockerignore`
# when it exists, so this file — not the review runner's — is what `mise run fue`
# uses. It is stricter for one reason: everything `ub init` is supposed to
# create must be absent, or the proof passes on state a new user does not have.
#
# `fnox.toml` is NOT excluded. It is committed, age-encrypted, and a new user
# gets it with the clone — running without the key is the path being tested.

.git
.github
.claude
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist

# Local state a run on this machine creates — the hub's and the MCP mirror's
# databases, a developer's own mise config. A new machine has none of it.
mise.local.toml
.mise.local.toml
data
**/data
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-*
*.sqlite3
*.db
.env
.env.*
*.bak

test-results
playwright-report
.DS_Store
.vite
